<title>BELGIUM: Belgian industrial output up 5.2% yr/yr in March.</title>
<headline>Belgian industrial output up 5.2% yr/yr in March.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Statistics Office released the following indices for production in industry excluding the construction sector -</p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION	    March 97   Feb 97	 March 96</p>
<p> work day index (1990=100) (*)   109.4	104.5	  104.0</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) index per working day, adjusted for length and composition of the months  </p>
<p> SEASONALLY ADJUSTED INDICES(*) March 97   Feb 97	 March 96</p>
<p> industry as a whole		  95.6	 95.1	   93.5</p>
<p> construction industry		78.5	 77.7	   76.2</p>
<p> investment goods		     99.3	100.0	   99.3</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) seasonally adjusted based on averages of the last 12 months.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
